# Owner DB Hardening 1-A

```yaml
id: OWNER-CARDINALITY-DB-HARDENING-1A
version: "2026-08-20"
status: LOCKED
phase: P1.3-C / Owner-DB-1A
authority: owner-cardinality-invariant.mdoc · users-rbac.policy.ts
decisions: [DEC-OWN-DB-001, DEC-OWN-DB-002, DEC-OWN-DB-003, DEC-OWN-DB-004]
related:
  - owner-cardinality-invariant.mdoc
  - ../../workspaces/denali/user-benefits-commercial-roadmap.mdoc
```

## Locked rule

Each tenant must have **exactly one** `UserTenant` with `role = owner` **and** `status = ACTIVE`, **except** the provisioning window with a pending owner invite (zero ACTIVE owners allowed until accept).

```text
isActiveOwner ⇔ role = owner AND status = ACTIVE
```

Suspended / non-ACTIVE `role=owner` rows do **not** count toward the unique index.

## Scope

| In | Out |
| -- | --- |
| Live data audit (staging first) | UI |
| Manual remediation plan (no auto-fix) | Discount / wallet / credit |
| Partial unique index migration | Owner lifecycle changes |
| Migration safety + tests | Triggers |

## Step 1 — Live data audit

**Runner:** `pnpm --filter @apps/api run audit:owner-cardinality`

**Requires:** `DATABASE_URL_ADMIN` (preferred) or `DATABASE_URL` with admin/bypass-RLS access.

**Queries (see `scripts/audit-owner-cardinality.sql`):**

1. Multiple ACTIVE owners per tenant
2. Zero ACTIVE owners **with** at least one membership (classify provisioning vs invalid)
3. Role distribution
4. Status distribution
5. Soft owners (`role=owner` AND `status <> ACTIVE`)

**Do not auto-fix.** Export findings for manual remediation.

## Step 2 — Remediation plan (manual)

| Finding | Recommended action |
| ------- | ------------------ |
| Multiple ACTIVE owners | Keep one canonical owner; demote others to `admin` (or agreed role) via controlled transfer/ops |
| Zero ACTIVE owners + pending `operator_pending_invites` with `role=owner` + `INVITED` | **Provisioning** — leave until invite accept |
| Zero ACTIVE owners + memberships, **no** pending owner invite | **Invalid active tenant** — assign/create owner via bootstrap invite or ops |
| Soft owners only | Allowed by index; ensure one ACTIVE owner exists for live tenants |

## Step 3 — Constraint design

After audit green (zero multi-owner tenants):

```sql
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS uq_user_tenants_one_active_owner
  ON user_tenants (tenant_id)
  WHERE role = 'owner' AND status = 'ACTIVE';
```

| Design choice | Lock |
| ------------- | ---- |
| Partial unique index | DEC-OWN-DB-001 |
| No trigger | DEC-OWN-DB-002 |
| No owner lifecycle change | DEC-OWN-DB-002 |
| Migration preflight fails on multi-owner | DEC-OWN-DB-003 |

## Step 4 — Migration safety

| Check | Status |
| ----- | ------ |
| Services already enforce invariant (P1.3-B) | Defense in depth — index is not the only gate |
| Transfer demotes previous owner **before** promoting target | Compatible with unique index (never 2 ACTIVE owners mid-tx) |
| Bootstrap / provisioning with 0 ACTIVE owners | Index allows zero matching rows |
| Index is defense in depth | DEC-OWN-DB-004 |

## Step 5 — Tests

| Test | Coverage |
| ---- | -------- |
| Migration SQL shape validation | Always-on |
| Postgres: second ACTIVE owner insert rejected | Requires `DATABASE_URL` + `DATABASE_URL_ADMIN` |
| Postgres: ownership transfer still works | Same |
| Memory: bootstrap owner invite (OWN-INT-06) | Existing wire suite |
| Memory: transfer yields one ACTIVE owner (OWN-INT-04) | Existing wire suite |

## Apply gate

| Environment | Gate |
| ----------- | ---- |
| Local / CI with empty or seeded clean data | Migration may apply |
| Staging / production | **Audit green first** — zero multi-ACTIVE-owner tenants |

## Decision index

| ID | Decision |
| -- | -------- |
| DEC-OWN-DB-001 | Enforce with partial unique index on `(tenant_id) WHERE role=owner AND status=ACTIVE` |
| DEC-OWN-DB-002 | No trigger; no owner lifecycle redesign |
| DEC-OWN-DB-003 | Migration preflight aborts if any tenant has >1 ACTIVE owner |
| DEC-OWN-DB-004 | Index is defense in depth; service policy remains source of product errors |
